        "original_id": "005fcff9-77c3-5a39-a3d5-a5b73e534d52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Dubuffet\n- Organizations: NME\n- Music groups: Art Brut, Franz Ferdinand, The Rakes, Bloc Party\n- Places: South London, Glasgow\n- Concepts: outsider art, Art Wave\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Dubuffet defined outsider art as art by prisoners, loners, mentally ill people, and other marginalized people, made without concern for imitation or presentation.\n- South London's Art Brut were named after Jean Dubuffet's definition of outsider art.\n- NME tagged South London's Art Brut as part of the Art Wave scene.\n- The Art Wave scene included The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand, and Bloc Party.\n- Franz Ferdinand are a Scottish rock band formed in 2002 and based in Glasgow.",
